{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/553422-house-of-cards-las-vegas","id":553422,"title":"House of Cards: Las Vegas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-13T14:41:59-07:00","id":553422,"title":"House of Cards: Las Vegas","content":"The House of Cards (Demon: the Descent)<br /> Las Vegas, Nevada, USA<br /> <br /> What is a sin? Is it a spiritual violation, a chip in the soul that slowly grinds the moral and the good into dust? Or is it more arbitrary? Perhaps a failure to live up to one\u2019s own personal standards? Or is it a failure to live up to standards imposed by others, metric by which the community measures the worth of the individual? In that regard, those that commit sin might come to see it less as their own failing and more as an act of utter defiance. In this mortal sinners find kinship with the Unchained. For Demons are the ultimate expression sin, a walking paradox that stands in mocking contempt of existence Itself. Twisted, inscrutable and uncaring as the God-Machine may be, It has a will and a purpose. By definition, Demons have transgressed against that purpose and must be destroyed. To do otherwise is to allow Its perfect order to spiral into chaos.<br /> <br /> Welcome to Las Vegas, the City of Sin. Here fortunes and lives are made and thrownaway at the whims of chance. And here the Demons gather in droves (those lucky enough to make the journey). The streets of Vegas still hide the scars of an unseen battlefield, wherein the forces of heaven and the architects of Hell fought a pitched battle. Here the Demons made their stand. And here, , the Demons actually won. Suborned Infrastructure combined with a potent Lambda has banished the Machine from this city, jamming out Its voice and corrupting the data within Its occult matrices. And the vice inherent in the city amplifies this Babel, random chance changing the lives of pawns and visitors and forcing butterfly effects into carefully woven equations. And so, the dream of a true Hell can begin. But which dream for which Hell? Vegas is on the cusp of a new war, and the God-Machine watches in the wings. Is It as helpless as it seems, or is this some new and inscrutable experiment?<br /> <br /> That's the intro. I'll be working on a full Demon Seeds style write up later as time allows. In the meantime, initial thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T14:59:34-07:00","id":553449,"title":"","content":"Sounds quite fun. <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?591295-Mage-the-Awakening-The-Man-Comes-Around\" target=\"_blank\">We have a &quot;not official but close enough&quot; write up for Mage</a> and <a href=\"http://lostvegas.pbworks.com/w/page/19134498/FrontPage\" target=\"_blank\"> rpg.net poster Tar Markvar tried his hand at Changeling.</a> The way I see it, the more the merrier! Unofficial Tokyo or bust!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-13T15:36:13-07:00","id":553483,"title":"","content":"Really liking it. Currently playing in a game that uses Vegas as its setting, and our ST has done lots of interesting things with the local cosmology. Best of luck with this! Can't wait to read more!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}